OL,3,GNEWSAMan praises surgeons for
OL,4,Areattaching severed thumb
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man has praised the "incredible" work
OL,7,Fof hospital staff who reattached his
OL,8,Fthumb after he accidentally cut it off
OL,9,Fwhile using a chop saw.
OL,11,FDaniel Parry, from Harrogate, had been
OL,12,Fhelping a friend with carpentry work on
OL,13,F15 October when the saw "kicked back"
OL,14,Fand "cut his thumb clean off".
OL,16,FAfter he took his thumb in a sandwich
OL,17,Fbag to Leeds General Infirmary, a team
OL,18,Fof surgeons worked through the night to
OL,19,Freattach it. By 17:00 BST the following
OL,20,Fday he was able to move it again.
OL,23,APub: 25-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,388,380,200,160,0,100
